affecting the code.

[1] Spaces, tabs and newlines.

[2] Preprocessor can have some rules on whitespace usage. Cannot 
remember what ANSI says about whitespace in macros. [3][4]

[3] Actually not, it's one space or newline. Combinations of consecutive 
spaces and tabs are changed to one space, trailing and leading spaces 
are eliminated and condsecutive newlines are changed to one newline.

[4] Is it something like this: preprocessor directives end with the next 
newline. A line-continuing character as the last character on the line 
within quotes (") or at the end of a line that started with preprocessor 
directive is deleted together with the follwing newline before 
whitespace compaction is done.

